{{!-- Security feed — a minified frontend for the sec-feed service
     (https://github.com/sredevopsorg/sredevopsorg-sec-feed), rendered as a block
     inside an existing page rather than as its own app.

     The whole block is gated on the `sec_feed_api_url` theme setting (Admin →
     Design → Theme): with it empty the island is not rendered, no chunk is fetched
     and no request is made, so the feature costs an unmodified site nothing. That
     also means the API origin can only ever come from the setting — there is no
     hardcoded host anywhere in the theme or in assets/js/islands/SecFeed.js, which
     is what keeps "the theme makes no third-party requests" true by construction
     rather than by review.

     What is rendered *here* rather than by the island:
       - the <section>, its heading and the frame: server-rendered, so they exist
         before the JavaScript does and cannot shift when it arrives;
       - a <noscript> link to the full feed, kept OUTSIDE the mount point because
         that element must stay empty (see assets/js/islands.js).
     The island owns only what the API decides: the status line, the tag filters,
     the rows and the footer link.

     TWO MODES, one partial. Every caller gets the same frame, heading and no-JS link;
     only the box around the island changes.

     * Embedded (the default, how partials/featured-row.hbs calls it): the frame is a
       bounded flex column. `h-full` makes it exactly as tall as the box that holds it
       (the 1/3 grid column that partials/featured-row.hbs pins this panel onto);
       `min-h-0` is what lets it be *shorter* than its content instead of being pushed
       open by it, because a flex item's automatic minimum size is its content;
       `flex-col` keeps the heading above the scroll region; `overflow-hidden` clips
       what the rounded frame would otherwise let poke out, and keeps the panel from
       becoming a second scrollbar next to the list's own.

     * Full page (`{{> "sec-feed" locale="en" full=true}}`, see page-secfeed.hbs): none
       of those apply. The section is an ordinary in-flow card, the mount point carries
       no height, and `data-fill="page"` tells the island to lay the widget out as a
       plain block rather than a column with a scroll region - the *document* scrolls
       and the list grows to its natural height. That is the whole reason the mode
       exists: the embedded flex contract (`flex-1` + `min-h-0` on the list) resolves
       against a bounded box, and in an auto-height one it would collapse the list to
       zero and make it scroll inside its own frame.

     In the embedded mode the mount point is a bounded box, not a scroll region, and
     that is deliberate: the island decides what scrolls. It lays the widget out as a
     flex column inside this box and lets the *list* take the remaining height and
     scroll, so the status line and the tag chips stay on screen while the reader
     scrolls twenty advisories. Putting the overflow on the mount point instead would
     have scrolled the chips and the footer away with the rows, and would have buried
     the status live region the accessibility story depends on. The two classes here
     are what make that possible: `flex-1` gives the island the height that is left,
     `min-h-0` lets it be shorter than its own content rather than pushing the panel
     open. See assets/js/islands/SecFeed.js for the other half of the contract.

     The `lg:absolute lg:inset-0` here only takes effect in the side-by-side layout,
     where partials/featured-row.hbs makes the column `lg:relative` and the column
     contributes nothing to the grid's row sizing. Below lg, and for any caller that
     just drops the partial into a page, no positioning applies and the panel is an
     ordinary in-flow block.

     Reuse: `{{> "sec-feed" locale="en"}}` from any template, or
     `{{> "sec-feed" locale="en" full=true}}` for the full-page variant. `locale` only
     picks the strings for the heading and the no-JS fallback; the island reads the
     page language for relative timestamps, which is why no locale is passed through.
     The block carries no vertical margin: partials/featured-row.hbs owns the rhythm
     for the side-by-side layout, and any other caller chooses its own spacing. --}}
{{#if @custom.sec_feed_api_url}}
<section class="{{#if full}}{{else}}lg:absolute lg:inset-0 h-full min-h-0 flex flex-col overflow-hidden {{/if}}rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-raised p-5" aria-labelledby="sec-feed-title">
  <div class="mb-1">
    <h2 id="sec-feed-title" class="text-sm font-bold tracking-wider text-strong uppercase">
      {{#match locale "=" "es"}}Inteligencia de seguridad{{else match locale "=" "br"}}Inteligência de segurança{{else}}{{t "Security feed"}}{{/match}}
    </h2>
  </div>

  {{!-- The island fills this and gives the list whatever height is left inside it, so
       the status line and the chips stay pinned above the scrollbar. `flex-1` is the
       part this template owns: the island's root only has a height because this box
       has one. `data-poll` is minutes between refreshes; it only polls while the tab
       is visible. --}}
  <div class="{{#if full}}{{else}}min-h-0 flex-1{{/if}}" data-island="SecFeed" aria-busy="true"
       data-api-url="{{@custom.sec_feed_api_url}}"
       {{!-- A full page shows as many advisories as the API allows (MAX_LIMIT in
            assets/js/lib/sec-feed-model.js, which clamps this anyway); the embedded
            block keeps the administrator setting. --}}
       data-limit="{{#if full}}25{{else}}{{#if @custom.sec_feed_items}}{{@custom.sec_feed_items}}{{else}}10{{/if}}{{/if}}"
       data-poll="5"{{#if full}} data-fill="page"{{/if}}></div>

  <noscript>
    <p class="mt-2 shrink-0 text-sm text-muted">
      {{#match locale "=" "es"}}
        <a class="text-brand-purple hover:text-brand-blue" href="{{@custom.sec_feed_api_url}}" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ver el feed de seguridad en vivo</a>
      {{else match locale "=" "br"}}
        <a class="text-brand-purple hover:text-brand-blue" href="{{@custom.sec_feed_api_url}}" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ver o feed de segurança ao vivo</a>
      {{else}}
        <a class="text-brand-purple hover:text-brand-blue" href="{{@custom.sec_feed_api_url}}" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{t "View the live security feed"}}</a>
      {{/match}}
    </p>
  </noscript>
</section>
{{/if}}
